{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DFrameBarAction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrameBarAction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.CharZero.Defs"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.bridgePhase_D_not_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.bridgePhase_D_not_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L188-L196","doc":"The defect vanishes only at `q = ±1`, never on the substrate where `q > 1`.\nSo the bar-oddness convention C enjoys is genuinely **unavailable** under D — not\nmerely unproved — and the cos-resummation's stated justification fails with it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.bridgePhase_D_bar_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.bridgePhase_D_bar_defect","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L175-L186","doc":"**Convention D: the phase is NOT bar-odd.** The defect is exactly\n`(q-1)²(q+1)²/(2q²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.bridgePhase_C_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.bridgePhase_C_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L163-L173","doc":"**Convention C: the phase is bar-ODD**, `α(u⁻¹) + α(u) = 0`. This is precisely\nthe hypothesis `prop:q-beta-cos-resummation` states as its justification — \"the bar\ninvolution maps `α ↦ -α`, so the resummation must be even in `α`\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume_D_invariant_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume_D_invariant_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L146-L159","doc":"Closed form for the D invariant:\n`V̂_D/q = ([2]_q + h²·z_D/q²)/2`, with `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` the quantum integer.\nIt is manifestly **not constant in `q`** — the content of Step 8: under D there\nis no fixed centre for a resummation to be built around. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume_D_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume_D_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L139-L144","doc":"**The convention-D bar-invariant is `V̂/q`** — the unique `q`-power rescaling\nfixed by bar, since the action carries weight `-2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume_C_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume_C_bar","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L125-L135","doc":"**Convention C: the bar action is an AFFINE REFLECTION** with fixed point `1`:\n`V̂(u⁻¹) = 2 - V̂(u)`. Contrast `tracedVolume_D_bar` — the same object, a different\ngroup action. That contrast is the whole content of Step 7. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume_D_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume_D_bar","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L113-L123","doc":"**Convention D: the bar action is MULTIPLICATIVE**, a weight `-2` eigenvector:\n`V̂(q⁻¹) = V̂(q)/q²`. Bar SCALES the traced volume; it has no fixed point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume_D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume_D","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L105-L111","doc":"Convention D, closed form: `V̂_D = (q⁴+1)/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.zD_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.zD_bar","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L92-L101","doc":"`z_D` is a bar-EIGENVECTOR of weight `-4`: `z_D(q⁻¹) = z_D(q)/q⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.hq_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.hq_bar","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L84-L90","doc":"`h` is bar-ODD: `h(q⁻¹) = -h(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.bridgePhase_eq_recentred_tracedVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.bridgePhase_eq_recentred_tracedVolume","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L75-L80","doc":"`α = (V̂ - 1 - h)/2`. A ring identity holding for EVERY `z`: the phase is the\ntraced volume re-centred on `1` and shifted by `h`. No hypothesis on `z` is used,\nwhich is exactly why the phase FORMULA is convention-independent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.inv_sq_add_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.inv_sq_add_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L66-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.two_ne_zero_cz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.two_ne_zero_cz","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L60-L64","doc":"`2 ≠ 0` in a characteristic-zero field. Needed because the bridge phase and\nthe invariant's closed form both divide by `2`; in characteristic 2 neither is\neven well posed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.comm_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.comm_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L55-L58","doc":"Helper: `q ≠ 0` and `q² + 1 ≠ 0` give `(q⁻¹)² + 1 ≠ 0`, since\n`(q⁻¹)² + 1 = (q² + 1)/q²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.bridgePhase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.bridgePhase","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L52-L53","doc":"The Q_β bridge phase `α = (z-1)h/2`, again with `z` free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.tracedVolume","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L47-L50","doc":"The Markov traced volume of the pp transfer matrix, `V̂ = z·h + 1`\n(`beta-decay-transfer-matrix-proof.md`: `V̂ = z·M₁₁ + M₂₁` with `T_pp = [[h,1],[1,0]]`).\nCarried with `z` FREE — a convention enters only when `z` is instantiated. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.hu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.hu","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L44-L45","doc":"`h` in the square-root variable: `h = q - q⁻¹ = u² - (u²)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.zC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.zC","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L39-L42","doc":"The convention-C Markov parameter in the square-root variable `u`, where\n`q = u^2`: `z_C = √q/(q+1) = u/(u²+1)`. Carried in `u` so the statement stays\nalgebraic — no `Real.sqrt`, no `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.zD","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L36-L37","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter `z_D = q³/(q²+1)` (owner ruling 2026-08-15 R1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DFrame.hq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DFrame.hq","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DFrameBarAction.lean#L33-L34","doc":"`h = q - q⁻¹`, the substrate difference. Convention-free. ","signatureChunk":0}]}